winemac: post the remote layer from the wine thread, not the cocoa one

macdrv_create_remote_layer posts WM_MACDRV_CREATE_REMOTE_LAYER through
NtUserPostMessage, which is a win32u call and needs a wine thread context.
0013 called it from inside publishRemoteLayer, which runs in an
OnMainThread block on the cocoa main thread, where that context does not
exist. The post never took effect and nothing after the CAContext
creation ran.

Measured on steam's webhelper, before and after, same runtime and bottle:

              before   after
  SEND enter      0       1
  SEND posted     -       ok=1
  RECV message    0       1
  CALayerHost     0       1

So the whole cross-process bridge was dead: the gpu process published a
valid CAContext every time and the owning process never heard about it.

publishRemoteLayer becomes prepare-only and exposes the hwnd and context
id; macdrv_publish_d3dmetal_remote_view does the post after OnMainThread
returns, back on the calling wine thread.

The window is still black after this, for a different and now visible
reason: the hosted layer arrives sized 0x0 because the client view the
receive side creates on demand is never given the client rect.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -430,6 +430,8 @@
 - (instancetype) initWithHwnd:(void*)hwnd frame:(NSRect)frame;
 - (BOOL) publishRemoteLayer;
 - (void) unpublishRemoteLayer;
+- (void*) remoteHwnd;
+- (CAContextID) remoteContextId;
 
 @end
 
@@ -1103,9 +1105,13 @@
         return NO;
     }
 
-    macdrv_create_remote_layer(_hwnd, _contextId);
+    /* the post is a win32u call and must run on the wine thread, not here on
+       the cocoa main thread; the caller does it after this returns */
     return YES;
 }
+
+- (void*) remoteHwnd { return _hwnd; }
+- (CAContextID) remoteContextId { return _contextId; }
 
 - (void) unpublishRemoteLayer
 {
@@ -4164,11 +4170,24 @@
     WineContentView* view = (WineContentView*)v;
     __block BOOL remote = NO;
 
+    __block void* hwnd = NULL;
+    __block CAContextID contextId = 0;
+
     OnMainThread(^{
-        if ([view isKindOfClass:[WineD3DMetalRemoteView class]])
-            remote = [(WineD3DMetalRemoteView*)view publishRemoteLayer];
+        if ([view isKindOfClass:[WineD3DMetalRemoteView class]] &&
+            [(WineD3DMetalRemoteView*)view publishRemoteLayer])
+        {
+            remote = YES;
+            hwnd = [(WineD3DMetalRemoteView*)view remoteHwnd];
+            contextId = [(WineD3DMetalRemoteView*)view remoteContextId];
+        }
     });
 
+    /* posted here, on the calling wine thread, so NtUserPostMessage has a
+       real thread context and actually reaches the owning process */
+    if (remote && hwnd && contextId)
+        macdrv_create_remote_layer(hwnd, contextId);
+
     return remote;
 }
 }
